# Goes in .github/CODEOWNERS. For each changed file, the LAST matching pattern decides its owners,
# so the catch-all comes first and the specific paths after it. With the ruleset's
# require_code_owner_review, a pull request needs an approval from the owners of every changed file.

# Everything else: the team that owns the application.
*                       @ORG/web-team

# Database migrations: a schema change can break the running version or lock a table.
/migrations/            @ORG/database-owners

# Infrastructure as code: Terraform, Kubernetes manifests, workflows that deploy.
/infra/                 @ORG/platform-team
/.github/workflows/     @ORG/platform-team

# Roles, policies and access rules.
/permissions/           @ORG/security-team

# Whoever can edit this file can remove the rules above: it needs the security team too.
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @ORG/platform-team @ORG/security-team
